**Gate:** all P0–P8 gates and installed-consumer checks pass at the identified candidate. The record can justify preferring Patamaps for the demonstrated workflows; deployment, registry publication, owner key/trust bootstrap and production activation require their own authorization. Performance superiority remains a separate empirical claim.

### Execution and evidence rules

Implementation should begin with P0. Keep `fixtures/conformance.json`, original reference files, migration expectations and historical raw records intact; add the obligation ledger rather than replacing old evidence. New schemas and byte domains require explicit version dispatch and regenerated contract artifacts. Every changed production module must enter the corresponding engine-identity calculation and acceptance binding.

Use proportional checks during feature work, then the complete P8/P9 gates for replacement. Existing Cargo format/Clippy/workspace tests, [source-integrity verification](scripts/test_source_integrity.py), reference drivers, generated-consumer controls and installation harnesses are starting points. Their current profile assertions must not be weakened or relabeled as full parity. Add a new parity verifier and new candidate receipts where existing snapshot-specific checks are insufficient.

Use unique retained run directories. Harnesses that automatically remove temporary trees must preserve their run material or obtain the owner's approval for a specific deletion list. Never remove project copies, caches, dependencies, histories or old evidence as a side effect of implementing or testing this plan. Report infrastructure-only harness changes separately from unchanged behavioral assertions.

The current ledger measures remaining obligations; it does not establish a reliable completion schedule or final public-surface denominator. P0 still requires reconciliation and classification, while the authorized implementation and verification work proceeds against this plan. The receipts above identify the executed candidate checks. Fresh platform acceptance, registry publication and production activation have not occurred as part of these parity repairs.
